    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d144">

                <pb facs="0299" n="195" xml:id="pg195"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Denby to Mr. Blaine</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1890-08-11"><hi rendition="#italic">August</hi> 11, 1890</date>.
                        (Received September 22.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1146.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inform you that since I
                    sent to you my dispatch No. 1125 of the 26th of July, relating to the Chi-nan-fu
                    troubles, I have received a communication from the American mission at that
                    place which furnished me the information I desired. This communication was sent
                    in advance of the receipt of the one sent to the mission by me.</p>
                <p>I have accordingly addressed to the foreign office a communication, of which I
                    inclose a copy.</p>
                <p>It will be seen that I strongly urge a full and final settlement of these
                    long-standing troubles.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Denby.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d144-a1.xml" xpointer="d144-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
